## Context

Filed at the author's request after a check for code that a library already
does better (2026-09-29). The finding is modest. Four parsers use pdfplumber
with layout-specific table logic that is research code and should stay:
`build_idn_cipp_priority_projects.py`, `build_idn_progress_priority_projects.py`,
`build_sen_plan_projects.py` and `_vnm_inventory.py` (pinned to 0.11.9). The
odd one out is `_senelec_annual_review.py`, which shells out to
`pdftotext -layout`. There is no shared opening helper and no text cache keyed
by the source hash.

This is below the severity floor: nothing is wrong in a deliverable. It is
labelled deferred; take it up when a new country parser is written, or
together with 1510.

## Actions

1. Settle on one extractor (pdfplumber, already a dependency), or document
   why the Senelec parser needs `pdftotext -layout`.
2. Add a shared helper that opens a snapshot by sha256 and caches page text
   keyed by hash and parser version.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every JETP parser opens PDFs through the shared helper.
- [ ] The parser outputs are byte-identical before and after the change.
